{"id":"word:hebrew:H4592","type":"word","title":"מְעַט","subtitle":"H4592 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"a little or few (often adverbial or comparative)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to מְעַט (H4592) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 101 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"מְעַט (mᵉʻaṭ) means a little or few (often adverbial or comparative) First listed occurrence: 1Chr 16 19."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"מְעַט","transliteration":"mᵉʻaṭ","pronunciation":"meh-at'","strong":"H4592","lemmaId":"hebrew:H4592","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["מְעַ֣ט","מְעַט","מְעַ֖ט","מְעָ֑ט","כִּ֭/מְעַט"],"morphs":[["HNcmsa",31],["HNcmsc",19],["HR/Ncmsa",17],["HTi/Ncmsa",7],["HD",5],["HAamsa",5],["HR/Aamsa",4],["HC/Ncmsc",2],["HR/Ncmsc",2],["HAampa",2]]},"definitions":{"short":"a little or few (often adverbial or comparative)","usage":"almost (some, very) few(-er, -est), lightly, little (while), (very) small (matter, thing), some, soon, × very.","full":"H4592. meat מְעַט 101 substantive a little, fewness, a few ; — ׳מ absolute and construct, מְעָ֑ט Isa 10:7 +, plural מְעַטִּים Psa 109:8 ; Eccl 5:1 ; &#8212; 1. a. Gen 30:30 לְפָנַי לך היה אשׁר מעט the little that thou hadst, 47:9 חיי שׁני ימי היו ורעים מעט few and evil, Lev 25:52 ; Num 26:54 (compare 33:54 ) נחלתו תמעיט וְלַמְעַט and to the small (few) thou shalt make small his inheritance, 33:56 ; 35:8 תמעיטו ַהמְעַט וּמֵאֵת , Deut 7:7 העמים מכלֿ ַהמְעַט אתם וכי ye are the fewest out of all peoples, 1Sam 14:6 בִמְעָ֑ט אוֺ בְּרַב לְהוֺשִׁיעַ , Jer 42:2 מֵהַרְבֵּה מְעַט נִשְׁאַרְנוּ כִּי we are left as few out of many, Ezek 5:3 בְּמִסְמָּר מְעַט מִשָּׁם וְלָקַחְתָּ , Hag 1:6 מְעָ֑ט וְהָבֵא הַרְבֵּה זְרַעְתֶּם (compare 1:9 ), Psa 8:6 מאלהים מעט ותחסּרהו , 37:16 לַצַּדִּיק מְעַט טוֺב (compare Prov 15:16 ; 16:8 ), 2Chr 29:34 לִמְעָ֑ט הָיוּ הַכֹּהֲנִים רַק ; as predicate Num 13:18 אִםרָֿ֑ב הוּא הַמְעַט , Josh 7:3 הֵמָּה מְעַט כִּי , Job 10:20 ; Ruth 2:7 ; Neh 7:4 ; Isa 16:14 מִזְעָר מְעַט וּשְׁאָר . — Hosea 8:10 מְעַט וַיָּחֵלּוּ and they begin as littleness ( = to be minished ) because of, &c.; but read probably ( ᵐ5 ) מִמְּשֹׁחַ מְעַט וְיֶחְדְּלוּ and they shall cease for a little ( d ) from anointing, etc. b. as substantive with following Genitive, Gen 18:4 מַיִם מְעַט a little of water , 24:17 , 43 , אֹכֶל מְעַט 43:2 ; 44:25 ; 1Sam 14:43 ; 17:28 הָהֵ֫נָּה הַצּאֹן מְעַט literally the fewness of those sheep, Prov 6:10 +; as Genitive to a previous substantive, מְעָ֑ט מְתֵי men of fewness Deut 26:5 ; 28:62 ; in apposition, Isa 10:7 מְעָ֑ט לֹא גּוֺיִם לְהַכְרִית , Ezra 9:8 מְעַט מִחְיָה , Neh 2:12 עִמִּי מְעַט וַאֲנָשִׁים , Eccl 9:4 ; either Genitive or appositive, 10:1 ; Dan 11:34 מְעָ֑ט עֵזֶר יֵעָֽזְרוּ with a help of smallness. c. twice declined as an adjective , Psa 109:8 מְעַטִּים יָמָיו יִהְיוּ , Eccl 5:1 מְעַטִּים דבריך יהיו עלכֿן . d. as adverb. accusative, of place , 2Sam 16:1 מְעַט עֹבֵר וְדָוִד ; of time, Job 10:20 b; of degree, 2Kin 10:18 מְעָ֑ט אֶתהַֿבַּעַל עָבַד אַחְאָב , Ezek 11:16 and have been to them for a sanctuary but little , Zech 1:15 ; repeated מְעַט מְעַט by little, by little = gradually, Exod 23:30 ; Deut 7:22 . e. phrases: — a. with the interr. הֲ , Gen 30:15 וְלָקַחַת אִישִׁי אֶתֿ קַחְתֵּךְ ַהמְעַט was thy taking my husband (too) little? and (wilt thou be) for taking also my son's love-apples? Num 16:9-10 כְּהֻנָּה גַּם וּבִקַּשְׁתֶּם ֗֗֗ הִבְדִּיל כִּי מִכֶּם ַהמְעַט is it too little for you that J. hath separated, etc., ... and do ye seek, etc.? 16:13 הִשְׂתָּרֵר גַּם תִשְׂתָּרֵר כִּי ֗֗֗ הֶעֱלִיתָנוּ כִּי ַהמְעַט , Josh 22:17 f. וגו תָּשׁוּבוּ וְאַתֶּם ֗֗֗ לָנוּ ׳ַהמְעַט , Isa 7:13 וגו תַּלְאוּ כִּי אֲנָשִׁים הַלְאוֺת מִכֶּם ׳ַהמְעַט is wearying men too little for you, that you will weary also my God? Ezek 34:18 (as Ew Co AV RV), Job 15:11 אֵל תַּנְחוּמוֺת מִמְּךָ ַהמְעַט . But Ezek 16:20 (si vera lectio) was it (too) little because of thy whoredom? (was that insufficient for thee? Kö iii. 406 m ). b. וְ מְעַט ׳עוֺד , Exod 17:4 וּסְקָלֻנִי מְעַט עוֺד yet a little, and they will stone me, Jer 51:33 ; Hosea 1:4 ; Psa 37:10 ; וְ מִזְעָר מְעַט ׳עוֺד Isa 10:25 ; 29:17 ; compare Hag 2:6 ; Job 24:24 . 2 כִּמְעַט like a little: hence a. within a little, almost (compare ὀλίγου ), Gen 26:10 ֗֗֗ שָׁכַב כִּמְעַט almost had lain ..., Psa 73:2 Qr, 94:17 ; 119:87 ; Prov 5:14 (all followed by perfect); Ezek 16:47 מֵהֶן וַתַּשְׁחִתִי קָט כִּמְעַט like a little , and thou hadst done more corruptly than they; Song 3:4 מֵהֶם שֶׁעָבַרְתִּי כִּמְעַט = hardly had I passed. b. with imperfect, just , 2Sam 19:37 עבדך יעבר כמעט just would thy servant pass over; lightly, easily, quickly (compare δἰ ὀλίγου ), Psa 2:12 אַמּוֺ כִּמְעַט יִבְעַר כִּי , 81:15 ; Job 32:22 . c. = shortly , 2Chr 12:7 . d. = little worth , Prov 10:20 רשׁעים ולב כמעט . e. pleonastic for מְעַט , Isa 1:9 (accents) שָׂרִיר כִּמְעָ֑ט a little remnant, Psa 105:12 (= 1Chr 16:19 ) בָּהּ וְגָרִים כִּמְעַט ; רֶגַע כִּמְעַט like the littleness of a moment = for a little moment, Isa 26:20 ; Ezra 9:8 .","rootNote":"or מְעָט ; from 4591 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 16 19","keyReferences":["1Chr 16 19","1Kgs 17 10","1Kgs 17 12","1Sam 14 6","1Sam 14 29","1Sam 14 43","1Sam 17 28","2Chr 12 7"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":101,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 16 19","book":"1Chr","chapter":16,"verse":19,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"כִּ/מְעַ֖ט","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"1Kgs 17 10","book":"1Kgs","chapter":17,"verse":10,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"מְעַט","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsc"},{"reference":"1Kgs 17 12","book":"1Kgs","chapter":17,"verse":12,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וּ/מְעַט","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Ncmsc"},{"reference":"1Sam 14 6","book":"1Sam","chapter":14,"verse":6,"englishText